{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>At the end of days.</b> From when they were born. A full year is called 'days,' because all the days return to their order as at the beginning, in their length and in their shortness." "<b>And Cain brought of the fruit of the ground.</b> From the leftovers of his food, as it is written, 'And it came to pass at the end of days <b>and Cain brought</b>' etc., after some time. Here Rashi explained: he brought flax seed. And therefore, 'to his offering He did not regard' — because he brought from the leftovers of his food and from the ground that was cursed; but Abel brought something important, before he partook of them, as it is written, 'from the firstborn of his flock and from their fat.' And because ruin came about through these two offerings, the Holy One, blessed be He, warned them that wool and linen should not be joined together."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:52.022614137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}